            <trans-unit id="oxjtEVt">
                <source>description.guided_project_pilot_card_edit</source>
                <target>Open a card, rewrite its title with a click, add or rename its steps, drag them into a new order, then duplicate it.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="poZvvnR">
                <source>description.guided_project_pilot_doc</source>
                <target>Find a reference, open it on its own page, then rewrite its title, its summary for a human and its detail for Claude.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="cNjx5cn">
                <source>description.guided_project_pilot_machine</source>
                <target>Give a machine its token, offer the actions it declares on your projects, then run one from a project's page.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="RyLb.eB">
                <source>description.guided_project_pilot_objectives</source>
                <target>Open a project, then write its objectives at the top of its page: what it aims at, at what pace, by when.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="G.IHxyv">
                <source>description.guided_project_pilot_plan</source>
                <target>Write the steps of a template once, offer it on its projects, then start a plan from a project's page: its cards follow each other.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="n.wECQG">
                <source>description.guided_project_pilot_runner</source>
                <target>A machine runs the card, then you validate its result or send it back with a comment.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="nevRENI">
                <source>description.guided_project_pilot_schedule</source>
                <target>Give a backlog card a date: it moves into the Planning.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="I01Y.bj">
                <source>description.guided_project_pilot_share</source>
                <target>Open a card, share it read-only, then give a link that lets edit it.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="VEI80xF">
                <source>description.guided_step_pilot_card_edit_drag</source>
                <target>Drag a step by its handle: when the card comes from a checklist template, the new order goes to the template and its other open cards.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="XGUl1Qp">
                <source>description.guided_step_pilot_card_edit_duplicate</source>
                <target>A copy of the card is made in the same project, its steps unticked, outside its plan.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="8tgamt5">
                <source>description.guided_step_pilot_card_edit_steps</source>
                <target>Type a step here to add it at the end of the list; a click on a step's text renames it, emptying it removes it.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="mCa1lTw">
                <source>description.guided_step_pilot_card_edit_title</source>
                <target>A click on the title opens it for typing, saved as soon as you leave the field; the markdown description, the reference and the awaited answer are edited the same way.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="jK5pb7k">
                <source>description.guided_step_pilot_doc_open</source>
                <target>A click on its tile opens it in a window, with its cards.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="jQPj5pE">
                <source>description.guided_step_pilot_doc_write</source>
                <target>Unfold « Edit the reference », change the title, the summary or the detail, then save.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="Vu1JcnP">
                <source>description.guided_step_pilot_machine_list</source>
                <target>The machines that run the actions, with their last call.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="oud4LXF">
                <source>description.guided_step_pilot_machine_new</source>
                <target>Name it: its token is shown once, to copy into the runner.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="zmGlAvo">
                <source>description.guided_step_pilot_machine_projects</source>
                <target>Once the machine has called, open each of its actions in the Actions screen and choose the projects offering it.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="RNr8Sop">
                <source>description.guided_step_pilot_machine_run</source>
                <target>On a project's page, its actions are buttons: one click hands a new card to the machine.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="7nj0XJN">
                <source>description.guided_step_pilot_objectives_open</source>
                <target>The pen of the Objectives section opens them, and creates them the first time.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="j0IR8u1">
                <source>description.guided_step_pilot_objectives_project</source>
                <target>Pick the project in the left column.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="QdWVHf5">
                <source>description.guided_step_pilot_plan_new</source>
                <target>Name it and write its steps, a {variable} being asked when the plan is created.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="ez9oqdZ">
                <source>description.guided_step_pilot_plan_projects</source>
                <target>Choose the projects whose page offers this template, then save.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="E.fh3mH">
                <source>description.guided_step_pilot_plan_start</source>
                <target>On one of these projects' page, choose the template and fill in its title and values.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="ne5jQTp">
                <source>description.guided_step_pilot_plan_template</source>
                <target>The templates list the steps a plan repeats, by hand or by a machine, and the ones each step waits for before it can be launched.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="oswwmeb">
                <source>description.guided_step_pilot_runner_entrust</source>
                <target>Pick an action of a machine online, fill in its parameters and hand it over.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="T4oflDI">
                <source>description.guided_step_pilot_runner_steps</source>
                <target>Each machine step has its button: launched one after the other, they run in turn and each one done is ticked. The handle reorders the steps, the order going to the card's template and its other cards.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="ni2dKdz">
                <source>description.guided_step_pilot_runner_validate</source>
                <target>Once the result is in, validate it, or send it back with a comment for another pass.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="LWkGxtg">
                <source>description.guided_step_pilot_schedule_due</source>
                <target>Leave it empty to send it back to the backlog.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="5mEj1oS">
                <source>description.guided_step_pilot_schedule_open</source>
                <target>Click its title.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="GQ73Hzr">
                <source>description.guided_step_pilot_schedule_save</source>
                <target>The card shows in the Planning on its date.</target>
            </trans-unit>
            <trans-unit id="EY0fTPI">
